#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# degree

#% text
# `degree(p, x)` gives the largest power of `x` in the polynomial `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `p` is expanded first, so cancelled terms do not count. The zero polynomial has degree `-inf`; a nonzero constant has degree 0.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
degree(x^3 + 2*x + 1, x)
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
degree((x + 1)^5 - x^5, x)
#% output
#= 4

#% cell
degree(5, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
degree(0, x)
#% output
#= -inf

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The degree in each variable:

#% cell
p = x^2*y^3 + x*y; [degree(p, x), degree(p, y)]
#% output
#= [2, 3]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The degree of a product is the sum:

#% cell
[degree((x^2 + 1)*(x^3 - x), x), degree(x^2 + 1, x) + degree(x^3 - x, x)]
#% output
#= [5, 5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `coefficient`, `coefficient_list`, `variables`
